# MACCHA publish allowlist — explicit curation for publish.sh.
#
# One repo-relative destination path per line. '#' starts a comment.
# A path naming a directory allows every file beneath it (recursive).
#
# Policy: FAIL-CLOSED. Anything in ~/bin/maccha or ~/INFRA that is not listed
# here is skipped and reported during publish — a brand-new local script is
# never public by default. Publishing a tool is therefore always a visible,
# committable decision instead of a side effect of a blind copy.
#
# The two local, gitignored configs (.publish-sanitize.sed, .publish-pii-words)
# still run on top of this: allowlisting decides WHAT may ship, they decide
# HOW it is rewritten and what aborts the publish.

